{{! ----- Set up ----- }}
<section id="admin-setup">
<h3>Set up</h3>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note local-unifiedgrader-help-note-req">
    <p><strong>Requirements.</strong> This page describes the plugin on <strong>Moodle 5.3</strong>.
    It needs Moodle 5.1 or later. On 5.1 and 5.2 late penalties and quiz due dates behave as they
    did in release 2.13; on Moodle 5.0, stay on release 2.13. Nothing else is required: every integration below is optional.</p>
</div>

<ol class="local-unifiedgrader-help-steps">
    <li><strong>Choose the activities.</strong> Assignments open in the grader by default. Switch
        on forums, quizzes and BigBlueButton under <a href="#settings-general">General</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Decide who marks.</strong> Editing teachers and managers can grade. Non-editing
        teachers cannot until you give their role <code>local/unifiedgrader:grade</code>
        (see <a href="#admin-capabilities">Capabilities</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Enable a document converter</strong> in Moodle if teachers should annotate Word
        files and online text (see <a href="#plugin-converter">Document conversion</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Set late penalty rules</strong> in Moodle's grade penalty settings, and take
        <em>Assignment</em> out of Moodle's own supported modules there
        (see <a href="#plugin-gradepenalty-duedate">Late penalty rules</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Optional:</strong> <a href="#settings-friction">Friction Feedback</a>, the
        <a href="#settings-integrity">report form and proctoring</a>, and a
        <a href="#settings-library">course code pattern</a> for the comment library.</li>
</ol>

<h4 id="feature-i18n">Languages</h4>
<p>The interface is translated into Afrikaans, German, Greek, Spanish, French, Hebrew, Italian,
Portuguese, Russian, Swahili, Xhosa and Zulu, as well as English. It follows each user's Moodle
language. This help page is in English.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Settings ----- }}
<section id="admin-settings">
<h3>Settings</h3>

<p>Go to <strong>Site administration &gt; Plugins &gt; Local plugins &gt; Unified Grader</strong>.
It opens an index with a tile for each group of settings. Each page links back to the index, and
the individual pages still turn up in the admin search.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.settings_index}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.settings_index}}" width="1300" height="555" loading="lazy"
             alt="The Unified Grader settings index with five tiles: General, Grading, Comment library, Friction feedback and Academic integrity, each with a one-line description.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The settings index: General, Grading, Comment library, Friction feedback, Academic integrity.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>All settings are stored under the <code>local_unifiedgrader</code> plugin. The name in
<code>code</code> below each label is the setting's key.</p>

{{! General }}
<h4 id="settings-general">General</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable for Assignments <code>enable_assign</code></th><td data-label="Default">On</td><td>Assignments open in the Unified Grader.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Replace submission comments <code>enable_submission_comments</code></th><td data-label="Default">On</td><td>Replaces Moodle's submission comments on the student's assignment page with the Unified Grader message thread, with notifications.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable for Forums <code>enable_forum</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>Forums open in the Unified Grader.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable for Quizzes <code>enable_quiz</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>Quizzes open in the Unified Grader.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable for BigBlueButton <code>enable_bigbluebuttonbn</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>BigBlueButton activities open in the Unified Grader, with recordings and Activity Points.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

