{{! Grading }}
<h4 id="settings-grading">Grading</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Render online text as PDF <code>onlinetext_as_pdf</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>Converts online text to a PDF so teachers can annotate it. Needs a document converter enabled in Moodle. When off, online text shows inline.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Allow manual grade override <code>allow_manual_grade_override</code></th><td data-label="Default">On</td><td>Teachers may type over the grade a rubric or marking guide calculated. When off, the grade always comes from the criteria.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable post grades for quizzes <code>enable_quiz_post_grades</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>Shows the post-grades control on quizzes. Posting the class switches <em>Marks</em>, <em>Maximum mark</em> and <em>Overall feedback</em> on in the quiz review options for the two <em>after the attempt</em> periods, and nothing else. Leave off if teachers manage visibility through review options.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Extension presets <code>extensionpresets</code></th><td data-label="Default">1, 2, 3, 7</td><td>The quick buttons in Dates &amp; extensions, as days after the due date, separated by commas. Multiples of 7 show as weeks.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Course name in the header <code>feedbackpdf_coursename</code></th><td data-label="Default">Course full name</td><td>Which name of the course is printed in the header of the feedback PDF: the full name or the short name. The footer of every page also carries the date the student's work was graded and the date and time the PDF was generated.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Quiz attempt must answer (%) <code>quizgenuineattemptpct</code></th><td data-label="Default">50</td><td>The share of a quiz's questions a student must answer for an attempt to count when deciding whether the quiz was late. An attempt submitted nearly empty is ignored. 0 counts every submitted attempt. Moodle 5.3 only.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The <em>Late penalties</em> part of this page also warns you while Moodle's own grade penalties
are still switched on for assignments.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
