</details>

{{! Friction feedback }}
<h4 id="settings-friction">Friction feedback</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Friction feedback <code>friction_enable</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>The site default. When on, a posted mark stays hidden from the student until they have read each part of the feedback. A teacher can force it on or off for an activity.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Seconds on each step <code>friction_seconds</code></th><td data-label="Default">20</td><td>How long a student waits on each part before they can confirm it. The timer pauses while the tab is in the background. 0 shows the confirmation at once.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Open held marks this many days before the course ends <code>friction_daysbeforeend</code></th><td data-label="Default">14</td><td>In a course with an end date, held marks are released once the course is this close to ending. 0 waits for the end date.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Open a held mark this many days after it was posted <code>friction_daysafterpost</code></th><td data-label="Default">21</td><td>A mark the student never opened is released this many days after posting. With a course end date as well, the earlier of the two wins. 0 releases on the next daily run.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Invitation <code>friction_invitation</code></th><td data-label="Default">Empty</td><td>One sentence shown at the start of the walk. Empty uses the built-in sentence: <em>Read the feedback on this step. Your mark follows once you have seen each part.</em></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The two day settings are a fail-safe. A held grade is in the stored course total, but Moodle
leaves hidden items out of the total a student sees, so a daily scheduled task opens held marks
when either limit is reached. A mark a teacher has hidden is left hidden.</p>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>See the Friction feedback page</summary>
    <div>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
