</details>

{{! Academic integrity }}
<h4 id="settings-integrity">Academic integrity</h4>
<p>The page opens with a note on plagiarism scanning: whether plagiarism plugins are enabled on
the site and where Moodle configures them. The Unified Grader has no plagiarism settings of its own.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Enable academic impropriety report form <code>enable_report_form</code></th><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td>With a URL below, the integrity button in the plagiarism card reads <em>Report academic impropriety</em> and opens the form as well as flagging the submission.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Report form URL template <code>report_form_url</code></th><td data-label="Default">Empty</td><td>The address of your form. These placeholders are replaced with URL-encoded values: <code>{studentname}</code>, <code>{studentid}</code>, <code>{coursecode}</code>, <code>{coursename}</code>, <code>{activityname}</code>, <code>{activitytype}</code>, <code>{gradername}</code>, <code>{graderurl}</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Proctoring services to show <code>proctoring_services</code></th><td data-label="Default">None</td><td>Tick Quilgo, ProctorLink, AutoProctor or SMOWL. A service that is not ticked is never contacted. Save, and the settings for each ticked service appear below.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">SMOWL: High priority alarms <code>smowl_red</code></th><td data-label="Default">Eight kinds</td><td>A student with any of these alarms is red. The defaults are: monitoring tool not launched, wrong person, more than one person, banned elements, suspicious behaviour, opened or used a program that is not allowed, and virtual machine.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">SMOWL: Alarms to leave out <code>smowl_ignore</code></th><td data-label="Default">None</td><td>These alarms do not affect the colour and are not listed. An alarm ticked in both lists counts as high priority.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">ProctorLink: High priority warnings <code>proctorlink_red</code></th><td data-label="Default">Three kinds</td><td>An attempt with any of these warnings is red. The defaults are: face does not match, more than one face, object detected.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">ProctorLink: Warnings to leave out <code>proctorlink_ignore</code></th><td data-label="Default">None</td><td>These warnings do not affect the colour and are not listed.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">AutoProctor: Low priority from this trust score <code>autoproctor_green</code></th><td data-label="Default">80</td><td>An attempt with at least this trust score (%) is green.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">AutoProctor: Medium priority from this trust score <code>autoproctor_yellow</code></th><td data-label="Default">50</td><td>An attempt with at least this score, and under the one above, is yellow. Anything lower is red.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Quilgo has no settings of its own here. See <a href="#admin-proctoring">Proctoring setup</a> for
what each service needs.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
