{{! ----- Capabilities ----- }}
<section id="admin-capabilities">
<h3>Capabilities</h3>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note local-unifiedgrader-help-note-warn">
    <p><strong>Only <code>grade</code> opens the grader.</strong> The Unified Grader item and the
    grader page are shown to users who hold <code>local/unifiedgrader:grade</code> in the activity.
    A non-editing teacher has <code>viewall</code> and <code>viewnotes</code> by default but not
    <code>grade</code>, so they see no Unified Grader item and cannot open the grader. Give their
    role <code>grade</code> if they mark.</p>
</div>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table local-unifiedgrader-help-table-stack">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Allowed by default</th><th scope="col">What it allows</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:grade</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Editing teacher, manager</td><td>Open the grader. Save grades, feedback, annotations and penalties, post grades, and change a student's dates.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:viewall</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Teacher, editing teacher, manager</td><td>Reserved. The grader reads it, but nothing depends on it at present. It does not open the grader.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:viewnotes</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Teacher, editing teacher, manager</td><td>Read teacher notes.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:managenotes</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Editing teacher, manager</td><td>Add teacher notes, and delete notes in the activity.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:viewfeedback</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Student, teacher, editing teacher, manager</td><td>Open the feedback page, download the feedback PDF, use submission comments, and complete the Friction Feedback walk.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:refer</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Editing teacher, manager</td><td>Flag a submission for an academic integrity review, and mark a referral resolved.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:viewproctoring</code></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Editing teacher, manager</td><td>See proctoring markers and the Proctoring card.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:sharecomments</code> <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-scope">site</span></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Editing teacher, manager</td><td>Copy a comment another teacher has shared into your own library.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:managesystemdefaults</code> <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-scope">site</span></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Manager</td><td>Maintain system-default tags and comments, and approve or reject teachers' suggestions.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>local/unifiedgrader:moderatelibraries</code> <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-scope">site</span></th><td data-label="Allowed by default">Manager</td><td>Open <em>Moderate comment libraries</em>, and export other people's libraries.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p>Capabilities marked <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-scope">site</span> are checked for
the whole site. The others are checked in the activity, so they can be changed for one course or
one activity. The grader also respects Moodle's own rules: a teacher without <em>Access all
groups</em> in a separate-groups activity sees and posts only their own groups.</p>

<p><strong>The Forum extension role.</strong> Unified Grader creates one role of its own,
<em>Forum extension (Unified Grader)</em>. It holds a single capability, Moodle's
<code>mod/forum:canoverridecutoff</code> (post to forums after their cut-off date), and it cannot
be assigned by hand. Unified Grader gives it to a student in one forum when their extension runs
past that forum's cut-off, and removes it when the extension ends. It shows in the student's roles
for that forum while it lasts. Do not edit or delete it; if it is deleted, it is created again when
next needed.</p>

<p>A marker who can open the report form but cannot <code>refer</code> gets a plain
<em>Report academic impropriety</em> link in the plagiarism card: the form, without the flag.</p>
</section>
